        {
            "schema": "shop_page",
            "days_ago": 60,
            "title": "Our Story",
            "slug": "about",
            "excerpt": "Ten years, one small shop and a lot of very good dogs and cats.",
            "featured_image": "@cat-dog-rest",
            "body": "<h2>Small on purpose</h2><p>Velvet Paw opened in 2014 as a single grooming table in the back room of a flower shop on Linden Mews. Word spread through the dog park, the florist moved across the road, and the back room became the boutique you can visit today.</p><p>We have grown slowly. Instead of stocking everything, we choose a short range of things we love — beds that survive years of naps, bowls that don’t slide across the floor, treats with ingredients you can pronounce — and we get to know the people who make them.</p><h2>How we look after animals</h2><ul><li><strong>One at a time.</strong> Grooming appointments are never double-booked, so nobody waits in a cage.</li><li><strong>Low-stress handling.</strong> Our team trains in fear-free techniques and takes breaks whenever a pet needs one.</li><li><strong>Honest advice.</strong> If something is better looked at by a vet, we will always say so.</li></ul><h2>Our journal</h2><p>Over the years our customers asked so many good questions that we started writing the answers down. You will find them, along with advice from trainers and vet nurses, in the <a href=\"{journal}\">Velvet Paw Journal</a>.</p>",
            "metadata": {
                "eyebrow": "About us",
                "subtitle": "A neighbourhood shop, *run by pet people*"
            }
        },
